# A client receives a 2500-byte event (three fragments), a 1025-byte event
# (two fragments, the last one byte), and a small event, out of order and with
# a duplicate. Each message is delivered once, in order, when its last
# missing fragment arrives.
endpoint client 0123456789abcdef 4800 1024 200000 0
recv 50003 
recv 50000 
recv 50002 
recv 50000 
> error duplicate
recv 50001 
> reliable 
> reliable 
> reliable 04010203
flush 80000
